    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0909" n="891" xml:id="pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.00/7–646</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Italian Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tarchiani</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-23">July 23, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of July 6, 1946,<anchor n="13" xml:id="d604-f1"/> informing
                    me that under date of June 28 the Italian Constituent Assembly, in compliance
                    with its institutional law, has elected Mr. Enrico De Nicola as provisional
                    Chief of State.</p>
                <p>It is also noted that the inaugural ceremony took place on July 1, when the
                    President of the Council, Mr. De Gasperi, who was acting as provisional
                    President, transferred the powers of the Presidency to Mr. De Nicola.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> F. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
